titive (HHI 0.01 across 544 companies in the universe; the top four hold 9% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 30% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 8% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 23% and a beta of 0.70, it is more defensive than the market, though its beta has shifted (1y -0.06 vs 5y 0.65), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $648.4M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 39% in the 2020 crash, 32% in the 2022 bear market and 59% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $286 (margin of safety -2%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 23%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $206 to $402 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Industrials peers: P/FCF 31.3 vs 22.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 45% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 3.2% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.9% (vs the 8% bar).","The 24 covering analysts target $331 on average, 14% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 16% clears the cost of capital of 7.6% by 9pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have been steady (CV 0.18).","It converts 22% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 7/9 and cash conversion of 1.30x.","ROE of 39% is amplified by 3.8x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 0.6% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.4x net debt to EBITDA ($1.3B of cash against $30.3B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 7.5x.","The current ratio of 0.91 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -0.5% over 3 years, 4.6% over 5 years and 1.2% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 27% of profits supports about 4.5% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -0.4% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Margins are expanding (+1.0% trend).","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.00 and a backlog worth 1% of annual revenue.","Capex runs 1.5x depreciation (15.5% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.1%), and institutions hold 92%.","It returns 3.4% a year to shareholders (1.6% in buybacks and 2.0% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.4% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 46 consecutive years, raising it 4.3% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 28,658 employees, each generates about $855K of revenue, 2.3x the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 3.5% a year.","That works out to $192K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $5.3M (6x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $5K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":69,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but no margin of safety; it becomes a buy below $243.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 46, gates 13/25)","ROIC 16.5% vs WACC 7.6%","FCF margin 22.4%","Piotroski F-score 7/9","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["Trades 2% above fair value of $286","P/FCF 31.3x vs sector 22.3x"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety"],"buy_below":242.74,"vc":{"base":285.57,"base_src":"dcf","bear":206.43,"bull":401.85,"alt_median":184.44,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.5483,"dispersion":0.2284,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 55% above the other models' median ($184)"]},"med":{"pe":23.2692,"ev_ebitda":13.319,"pfcf":22.2778,"pb":3.0551,"roic":0.1001,"gross_margin":0.2851,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0147}},"ticker":"UNP","date":"2026-11-06"}